@rikbosch Thanks for the repro, I was able to use it and create a PR.

The logs you see were just type loading warnings and not errors, types are getting generated for that assembly. I enhanced the warning logging method to only output when we encounter any other type of exception, but not BadImageFormatException.

Thanks for reporting.

@rikbosch thanks for the additional info, I was able to repro it this way, I updated my PR with a fix.

I don't know why your state class in ```Grain<T>``` needs a sql connection, generally I think persistence would happen at the grain level and ```<T>``` should be a POCO or alike.

On the other hand in your situation, you can have an ```IDbConnection``` there which is not causing any problem with the currently released 2.0.0-beta1 bits.
